# Thai date display

When showing dates to users in GoldenSoft HR (and related suite UIs), use **Thai Buddhist-era** format — not ISO and not Gregorian CE in the UI.

## Rules by surface

| Surface | Helper | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **Person + date cards / approval lists** | `formatThaiDateReadable` / `formatThaiDateRangeReadable` | `3 ก.ค. 2569`, `3-5 ก.ค. 2569` |
| **Notifications / feedback messages** | same readable helpers (+ `formatThaiDateTimeReadable` for “แจ้งเมื่อ”) | `ลา 3-5 ก.ค. 2569` |
| **Forms / ThaiDateInput** | `ThaiDateInput` (shows `DD/MM/BBBB`) | `18/06/2569` |
| **Dense formal meta** (optional) | `formatThaiDate` / `formatThaiDateRange` | `18/06/2569` |

Range rules for readable helpers:

- Same day → one date only
- Same month → `3-5 ก.ค. 2569`
- Cross month/year → `28 ก.ค. – 5 ส.ค. 2569`

## Storage / API

Keep ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` (ค.ศ.). Never show raw `2026-06-18` in user-facing copy.

## How to implement (HR)

```ts
import {
  formatThaiDateReadable,
  formatThaiDateRangeReadable,
  toIsoDate,
} from "@/lib/hr/thai-date";
import ThaiDateInput from "@/components/hr/thai-date-input";

formatThaiDateReadable(row.workDate); // "3 ก.ค. 2569"
formatThaiDateRangeReadable(row.startDate, row.endDate); // "3-5 ก.ค. 2569"
<ThaiDateInput value={iso} onChange={setIso} />
```

Person+date card layout also follows `.cursor/rules/hr-person-date-cards.mdc`.
